This project was written from scratch. No source code was copied from the projects
below; it borrows ideas and design patterns from them, credited here.

toolsmelt
  https://github.com/sepehr071/toolsmelt (MIT)
  Borrowed: introspect an existing system first (database schema, API spec) and design a
  small set of reviewed actions from it instead of exposing everything; strict schemas where
  unknown keys are errors; read-only vs write separation; secrets referenced by env var name.

Pomerado
  https://github.com/Pomerado/pomerado (MIT)
  Borrowed: the planned website adapter's approach (explore a site, complete one worked
  example, generalise it into a deterministic integration instead of live computer use).
  Only the connector slot exists in this version.

LoomFlow
  https://github.com/banmu123/LoomFlow (MIT)
  Borrowed: natural language -> runnable workflow JSON that a person reviews and edits before
  it runs; a single registry as the source of truth for what nodes/actions exist, validated
  automatically.

agent-safe-pipeline (Decionis AgentSafe)
  https://github.com/decionis/agent-safe-pipeline (Apache-2.0)
  Borrowed: a gate in front of every consequential action with three outcomes
  (ALLOW / ESCALATE / BLOCK), fail-closed defaults, approvals bound to the exact action
  payload and executed at most once, and a decision record for every action.

google-docs-markdown-sync
  https://github.com/rsheyd/google-docs-markdown-sync (MIT)
  Borrowed: keep machine state (cursors, hashes) out of the user's documents, track what
  was already synced so retries do not duplicate rows, and treat the sheet's header row as
  the stable mapping contract.

Runtime dependency
  mysql2 (MIT) https://github.com/sidorares/node-mysql2
